Sad, familiar tale of a YASD:

I did down to sokoban, up to grab an amulet of
reflection, back down to Mines Town, still at
XP:1/17.

Mines Town was a fun bones level, inherited via
Hearse, with a priestess of Athena wandering around
the level, but the altar an altar to Hermes.

The priestess was peaceful, and (knock me down with
a feather) accepted my donations out there in the
hallway.

I got there with over 10,000z, cleaned out a couple
of shops while I could still find her, ended up with
naked AC:-3 purely from donations, cleaned out two
more shops but never saw the priestess again. [I
didn't have telepathy, she may just have outrun me.]

I glommed a huge stash of stuff that some monster
had grabbed in Mines Town and fallen to the next
level down, soon was kitted up with +1 Silver Dragon
scale mail, a nice +3 leather hat, gauntlets of
power, a heavy shield, speed boots, an oilskin cloak.

I found/created a game total of around 26 blessed
potions of water.

Based on bones piles and luck and clearing curses, I
had two blessed bags of holding, a magic whistle,
four surviving pets, AC:-23.

I found four different kinds of grey stones in the
game, so those were my first ID attempt. I'd
expended a prayer to get rid of the Loadstone.

I'd found and then blessed both a luckstone and a
touchstone and had my second blessed ID identify
my scrolls and rings and wands, and the touchstone
ID my gems.

I had IDed /oInvisible and /oTeleport, so
/oCancelation was a gimme when I'd see it, my BoH
were safe.

Even though I didn't need the luckstone, I was
feeling good enough to do Mines end, and hadn't been
down there in a long time, so I did. It was the
really easy, Gnome King's Wine Cellar version,
giving me lots more potions to dip into the pools in
Mines Town I'd made from the fountain there after
the watch suffered various pet-related inconveniences.

    It's pretty easy to take the watch captain when
    his long sword is cursed, he's peaceful toward
    me, and I have two leashed maxed-out cats to
    drag with me to wherever he goes, in unrelenting
    attack. Having two pets means they split the
    HP damage he causes, and survive, where going at
    him one at a time, giving him time to heal in
    between, they usually die.

Having done the Sokoban and Mines Town gigs, I
wasn't paying attention to keeping my XL low, ended
up doing a bunch of stash IDing work in the Mines
Town temple at XL 11 after a Gnomish Mines Incubus
helped things along. I was also slowing working
through my Bag of Tricks, create monsters wands
(four of them), and create monster scrolls, just to
keep Hermes receptive to various prayers (I ended
up praying nine times during the game).

By dint of sheer "playing after getting enough
sleep", I managed not to eat, and choke, while
satiated.

Well, with the priestess gone missing

    she may have been killed by my pets, or simply
    evaded me, but I think she either evaporated
    along with my more than 20,000z in donations, or
    fell down a hole and was never seen again

every other time or so that I'd enter the temple, a
huge ghost (including once the ghost of my quite
living PC, that was weird) would appear, keeping my
pets and I busy in battle far more often than would
have been the case for randomly generated monsters.

The pets's HPs were headed south.

I went to cast healing on a needy pet, (you can see
where this is going, right?) had to take off a bunch
of intefering armor to do so.

Sure thing, I'm in Mines Town at DLVL 8, I'm XL 11,
so in the door marches a cockatrice.

A flurry of +3 blessed daggers does for the beast
quickly enough, I go to pick up my daggers and the
handy rubber chicken, and leave a new statue in the
temple.

Yes, gauntlets of power are bad inteferers with
spells, yes, I forgot I'd just taken off my gloves.

This may have been my best ascension chance in two
years, even though, the Wenchess of Athena having
gone a-scamper with all my money, my score table
slot was only 18th/100, NetHack scoring being so
biased toward the zorkmid in the hand as it is.

Grrr. Why am I so astonishingly stupid every time I
touch the keyboard to play NetHack???

Moral: Note to self: keep your XL low until you need
XL:14 for the quest, you'll live a lot longer, Kent.

NB: rust monsters are a lot less annoying when you
